      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author encodes two-counter-machine computation in interacting identical timed processes with only one clock and one timing parameter. Global reachability forces all process copies to attain the target, allowing the construction to detect incorrect timing choices and extra processes even without invariants. The full synchronization/gadget and global-target argument is retained. This is an independent negative main result; no simulation lemma, alternative invariant case or direct consequence is counted separately.",
